  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "trip-hop: a slow, heavy breakbeat — kick one and the a of two and three-and, a big snare on two and four — with swung eighth hats and a dark, held bass that moves once a bar",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars: kick one, two-a, three-and; one, one-and, three-and; the snare on two and four at full weight with a ghost before the second; eighth hats swung and a little behind the beat. The bass holds the root for most of a bar and steps down a third at its end. Played under the Downtempo key at 96-100: trip-hop wants 75-94, where no band is (the house band starts at 95)."
  }
